.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt LSBOM 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm lsbom
.Nd list the contents of a bill of materials
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl b
.Op Fl c
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl l
.Op Fl m
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl x
.Op Fl p Ar parameters
.Ar bom ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A bill of materials
.Pq Pa .bom
records the files an installer package lays down.
.Nm
prints one line for each path in it:
.Bl -tag -width "symbolic links" -compact
.It directories
path, mode, uid/gid
.It files
path, mode, uid/gid, size, checksum
.It symbolic links
path, mode, uid/gid, size, checksum, target
.It devices
path, mode, uid/gid, device number
.El
.Pp
The modes are in octal, the fields separated by tabs.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b , c , d , f , l
Only block devices, character devices, directories, files or symbolic
links; several may be given.
.It Fl m
Also the modification time of files.
.It Fl s
Only the paths.
.It Fl x
No modes for directories and symbolic links.
.It Fl p Ar parameters
Print the fields named, in that order:
.Cm c
checksum,
.Cm f
path,
.Cm F
path in quotes,
.Cm g
group id,
.Cm G
group name,
.Cm m
mode in octal,
.Cm M
mode as
.Xr ls 1
shows it,
.Cm s
size,
.Cm S
size in K or M,
.Cm t
modification time,
.Cm T
modification time as a date,
.Cm u
user id,
.Cm U
user name,
.Cm /
uid/gid,
.Cm \&?
user/group names.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkgutil 1
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
